Algility started in 2024 on one bet:

SMBs don't fail because they lack tools. They fail because five tools don't talk, and a human becomes the glue.

That human is expensive. Slow. Inconsistent. And somehow still the "process."

So we don't sell another dashboard to stare at. We build AI-native systems for sales, growth, and customer acquisition. On the stack you already pay for. CRM. Inbox. Airtable. Zapier. OpenAI. Claude. The Python job somebody wrote at 1am and prayed would hold.

Buying another SaaS seat feels like progress. It usually isn't. It's shopping.

Real progress looks boring. Lead comes in. Follow-up fires. Handoff doesn't die in Slack. Nobody copy-pastes between five tabs like it's a personality trait.

Rule: if a workflow needs a hero every day, you don't have a system. You have a job.

Algility exists to replace the hero with infrastructure. Systems compound. Tools just sit there waiting for someone to click them.
